{"author":{"id":"fb9734b7331903226ef3f5df545b960dd5ac64d18b49faee11e8b8e0bd561c91"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1783542864,"nonce":"xBvM50o41bykKIAMrrDjCF3yVNs=","title":"Pinned arena Phase 3: extend to training + model-agnostic seam","message":"Extend the persistent pinned weight arena (534ea49) to cover TRAINING, and make the machinery usable by any streamed model rather than Krea2-only. Full spec + plan: tasks/open/PINNED_ARENA_PHASE3_TRAINING.md.\n\nStarting point (2026-07-08): sampling arena works end-to-end and is validated on the real 768px fp8 Krea2 smoke; the arena core, _build_pinned_arena, try_borrow_pack, pack_block_host[_from_flat], the pin-budget chain, and the trainer enable seam are already model-agnostic. Training still pins its frozen base through a SEPARATE owned mechanism (enable_ingraph_training), mutually exclusive with the arena (krea2.py:756 gates use_pinned_arena = pinned_arena AND NOT ingraph_training).\n\nGoal: training streams its frozen base from the SAME persistent arena the sampler uses (one pin for the whole run, no separate ingraph_training pin, no train\u003c-\u003esample repin churn), with LoRA composed on top (base = borrowed frozen source, grads to resident LoRA only).\n\nSlices:\nA (prerequisite, perf): make the eager/pre-compile streaming bypass recognize register-pinned arena flats. _profile_is_pinned (manager_modules.py:165) and bounce_pool.py:91 gate on torch is_pinned(), which is False for cudaHostRegister flats; streamed leaves are VIEWS into the flat so is_host_pinned's exact-ptr table lookup also misses them. Prefer O(1) module/leaf tagging over a hot-path range scan. Without this, training's non-ingraph forwards stream arena weights through bounce staging anyway.\nB: flip the krea2.py mutual exclusion; enable_ingraph_training borrows the arena (mirror enable_ingraph_sampling), LoRA composition unchanged. Validate frozen-FP8-base-borrowed + trainable-bf16-LoRA + backward numerically vs owned-pin. Assert no arena-repointed leaf is requires_grad at optimizer-build time.\nC: extract the borrow-or-own pack loop into a shared ingraph_stream helper (build_or_borrow_block_packs), document the ingraph arena protocol (freeze base -\u003e plumb flag -\u003e enumerate blocks -\u003e enable via helper); prove with a synthetic non-Krea2 multi-block module.\nD: validate on smoke_krea2_train_cuda.py --pinned-arena with ingraph training + a full train-\u003esample-\u003etrain cycle; then consider flipping the default.\n\nRelated: 534ea49 (arena, sampling done), da1aae5 (pin manager authority), 3ca8a7b (in-graph streaming), f1c45ae (FP8-native training gate).","files":null}]}